menu "Moby firmware"

config MOBY_F3_USB_LINK
    bool "Enable the F3 USB control link"
    depends on !MOBY_F2_MIC_TEST
    default y
    help
        Talk the Moby control protocol over the USB-Serial-JTAG port: pairing,
        heartbeats, expression and display text commands. The port carries
        frames only and the console stays on UART0. No audio is ever sent in
        this stage. The F2 microphone bench image does not include the link.

config MOBY_F4_PTT_AUDIO
    bool "Enable F4 push-to-talk audio stream (microphone)"
    depends on MOBY_F3_USB_LINK && !MOBY_F1_LED_TEST
    default n
    help
        Stream the INMP441 microphone to the paired, authenticated desktop while
        the Talk button is held and the hardware mute switch lets the microphone
        path through. Advertises the usb_pcm capability. The microphone clocks
        are off at all other times, the red LED is lit exactly while the
        microphone runs, and nothing records on boot, in pairing, without a
        session, or after a disconnect. Off by default: the default image has no
        audio code at all (see docs/adr/0002-f4-push-to-talk.md).

config MOBY_F1_LED_TEST
    bool "Enable F1 bench test for the red LED"
    default n
    help
        During a bench test, turn on GPIO21 for an accepted Talk press while
        the physical switch enables the microphone path. Disable before normal use, where
        the red LED is reserved for an audio capture session.

config MOBY_F2_MIC_TEST
    bool "Enable F2 bench test for the INMP441 microphone"
    depends on !MOBY_F1_LED_TEST
    default n
    help
        Capture while Talk is held and the physical microphone path is enabled.
        Report aggregate PCM levels over UART after an authorized bench capture.

endmenu
